# Stripe

| Package | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `@nu-art/stripe-shared` | `ApiDef_Stripe` (checkout, portal, webhook), `ApiDef_StripeAdmin` (customer, coupons, promotion codes), request types, `appUrl` |
| `@nu-art/stripe-backend` | `ModuleBE_Stripe`, `ModuleBE_StripeAPI`, `RtdbStripeEventLedger`, hooks |
| `@nu-art/stripe-frontend` | `ModuleFE_Stripe.startCheckout()` / `openPortal()`, admin callers |

## Backend setup

- Secrets, stored raw in Secret Manager and read lazily on first use: `stripe-secret-key` and `stripe-webhook-secret` (names are configurable).
- Config: `appBaseUrl` (success, cancel and return paths are app-relative and joined to it; absolute URLs are refused) and `allowedPriceIds` (a client can only choose from these).
- Call `ModuleBE_Stripe.setCustomerResolver(async () => ({customerId?, email?, clientReferenceId?}))` from the app. Map the session to a customer there, and throw when nobody is signed in.
- Add `ApiDef_Stripe.webhook` to the app's open APIs. It is authenticated by the Stripe signature.
- The webhook route is registered with `{rawBody: true}`, so the global body parsers skip it. The handler reads the exact bytes from the stream, capped at 1 MB. On Cloud Functions it uses `req.rawBody` instead.

## Webhooks

- Verify the signature, claim the event id in RTDB (`/state/ModuleBE_Stripe/events/<id>`, transaction), dispatch hooks, mark the event done.
- A redelivered event is skipped. A hook that throws releases the claim, so Stripe's retry processes it again. An unfinished claim expires after `eventClaimLeaseMs`.
- Hooks, implemented on any module:
  - `OnStripeEvent.__onStripeEvent(event)`: every event.
  - `OnStripeCheckoutCompleted.__onStripeCheckoutCompleted(session, event)`.
  - `OnStripeSubscriptionChanged.__onStripeSubscriptionChanged(subscription, event)`: created, updated and deleted.
- Hooks must be idempotent per object state (Stripe can deliver events out of order). Read `subscription.status` rather than counting events.

## Checkout options

`StripeCheckoutRequest.allowPromotionCodes` and `paymentMethodCollection` (`always` | `if_required`) are optional. Omitted, they are not sent, so Stripe keeps its own defaults. When set, checkout passes them as `allow_promotion_codes` and `payment_method_collection`.

`automaticTax` and `taxIdCollection` are optional. Omitted or false, they are not sent. `automaticTax: true` sends `automatic_tax: {enabled: true}` and `billing_address_collection: 'required'`. `taxIdCollection: true` sends `tax_id_collection: {enabled: true}`. When the resolver returns a `customerId`, checkout also sends `customer_update`: `address: 'auto'` for automatic tax and `name: 'auto'` for tax id collection. Stripe rejects those features on an existing customer without that update. A session that only has `customer_email` does not send `customer_update`.

## Customer

`ModuleBE_Stripe.updateCustomer({customerId, email?, invoiceEmail?})` updates the Stripe customer. `email` is the customer email. `invoiceEmail.locales` is the ordered locale list Stripe uses for invoice and receipt emails (`preferred_locales`). At least one of those two must be set. The same call is `ApiDef_StripeAdmin.updateCustomer`.

## Coupons and promotion codes

Admin routes, same auth as the rest of the API (do not add them to openApis):

- `createCoupon` / `listCoupons` / `deleteCoupon` — a coupon is either `percentOff` or `amountOff` plus `currency`. `metadata` and `appliesToProducts` are optional on create (`applies_to.products`). The coupon view includes `timesRedeemed`, `metadata`, `maxRedemptions`, `redeemBy` and `appliesToProducts`.
- `listCoupons` pages with `limit`, `startingAfter` and `endingBefore`. `metadata` (for example `{app: 'booking'}`) keeps only coupons whose metadata contains those pairs. Stripe's list has no metadata filter, so the module scans forward and the next cursor is the last returned coupon id. `hasMore` is true when another match exists. A metadata filter cannot be combined with `endingBefore`.
- `createPromotionCode` / `listPromotionCodes` / `updatePromotionCode` — a promotion code points at a coupon with `{promotion: {type: 'coupon', coupon}}`. The view includes `firstTimeTransaction`. `listPromotionCodes` pages with `startingAfter` and `endingBefore`. `updatePromotionCode` sets `active`. Pass `couponMetadata` to refuse the update unless the coupon metadata matches, which is how a deactivate checks that the coupon belongs to an app.

Direct module methods take the same shared types.
